OVERVIEW: Extract raw pixel values from DICOM images

USAGE: dicom-measure pixel <file-path> [--output <output>] [--format <format>] [--unit <unit>] [--force] [--verbose] --point <point> [--frame-number <frame-number>] [--frame <frame>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to the DICOM file

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path (prints to stdout if omitted)
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: text, json, csv (values: text, json,
                          csv; default: text)
  --unit <unit>           Unit for measurements: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels
                          (physical units need a pixel spacing; see the
                          overview) (values: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels;
                          default: mm)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --point <point>         Point to sample as x,y (e.g., 150,150)
  --frame-number <frame-number>
                          Frame number, 1-based (PS3.3 Table 10-3: the first
                          Frame is Frame number 1); at most Number of Frames
                          (0028,0008). Default 1
  --frame <frame>         Deprecated: 0-based index; use --frame-number (index
                          0 is Frame number 1)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

